  "output": {
    "answer": "Two things, from the record. First, new behavior ships behind a flag that defaults off, and only a human flips it to production, explicitly, the next morning — never as a side effect of a lane finishing; production isn't pre-approved by an overnight run. Second, there's a standing rule that a reviewer one tier above the author has to sign off — self-approved merges aren't allowed. So a gate clearing lets work merge into the lane's own branch and unlocks the next experiment, but it doesn't put anything live or let the agent approve its own change.",
